      "result_inner_catx": "ValueError: No catdef JSON document at ZIP root — HARD REJECT",
      "result_legacy_inner_catx_envelope": "accepted; envelope keys seen ['catx','type']; 1 item, 1 media member",
      "result_legacy_inner_dual_envelope": "accepted; envelope keys seen ['catio','catx','type']; 1 item, 1 media member",
      "finding_that_corrected_this_seat": "This seat had weighted the envelope key as the hard break in its first reading of the rulings. The test showed otherwise: the envelope key is a soft break and the inner member name is the hard one. Recorded because the correction is the useful part.",
      "cta_recheck": "catdef.org/fetch against the canonical bundle, cache-busted: 502 'Upstream body is not valid UTF-8'. Controls: plain JSON via /fetch 200; bundle direct from GitHub 200, 1,680,109 bytes. Renderer at render.catdef.org serving build 001, 36329 bytes, sha256 prefix 35e53d14d2d5d098 — unchanged since the CA-019 step-4 promotion."
    },
    "open_spec_question_raised_not_decided": "ft-catx-05: when both catio and catx envelope keys are present and disagree, which governs? Dual-stamping makes disagreement reachable in normal operation. This seat recommends catx wins. It is a recommendation for the Director, not a ruling, and no reader should implement a precedence rule before it is ruled.",
